# State Management - Complete Reference

## Pinia Stores

### 1. Auth Store (`stores/auth.ts`)

**State**:
```typescript
{
  user: User | null;          // Firebase user object
  idToken: string | null;     // JWT token for API requests
  loading: boolean;           // Initial auth check in progress
}
```

**Getters**:
- `isAuthenticated`: Returns true if user exists
- `userId`: Returns user UID

**Actions**:
- `init()`: Initialize auth listener (called in main.ts)
- `login(email, password)`: Sign in with Firebase Auth
- `logout()`: Sign out
- `refreshToken()`: Get fresh JWT token

**Router Integration**: 
- Route guard checks auth state
- Redirects to /login if not authenticated
- Redirects to / if authenticated user visits /login

### 2. Clips Store (`stores/clips.ts`)

**State**:
```typescript
{
  items: Clip[];              // Current page of clips
  total: number;              // Total count across all pages
  page: number;               // Current page number
  pageSize: number;           // Items per page (from config)
  selectedGame: string;       // Active game filter
  searchText: string;         // Search query
  selectedTags: string[];     // Active tag filters
  publishedFilter: boolean | null;  // null = all, true = published only, false = unpublished only
  starredFilter: boolean;     // Filter starred clips
  loading: boolean;           // Request in progress
  abortController: AbortController | null;  // For canceling requests
  requestId: number;          // Track latest request
}
```

**Getters**:
- `totalPages`: Total pages based on page size
- `hasNextPage`: Can load more pages
- `hasPreviousPage`: Can go to previous page

**Actions**:
- `fetchClips(append)`: Load clips with current filters (append = add to existing)
- `loadMore()`: Increment page and append results
- `updateClip(clip)`: Update single clip in items array
- `removeClip(clipId)`: Remove clip from items array
- `setGame(game)`: Set game filter and reload
- `setSearch(query)`: Set search filter and reload
- `setTags(tags)`: Set tag filters and reload
- `setPublishedFilter(published)`: Set published filter and reload
- `setStarredFilter(starred)`: Set starred filter and reload
- `resetFilters()`: Clear all filters and reload
- `resetPagination()`: Reset to page 1
- `goto(page)`: Jump to specific page
- `nextPage()`: Go to next page
- `previousPage()`: Go to previous page

**Request Handling**:
- Cancels previous request when new one starts
- Uses requestId to handle race conditions
- Only updates state if request is still current

### 3. Collections Store (`stores/collections.ts`)

**State**:
```typescript
{
  items: Collection[];        // All collections
  clipsState: {
    currentCollectionId: number | null;
    items: Clip[];            // Clips in current collection
    total: number;            // Total clips in collection
    page: number;             // Current page
    pageSize: number;         // Items per page
    loading: boolean;         // Request in progress
    abortController: AbortController | null;
    requestId: number;
  }
}
```

**Actions**:
- `fetchCollections()`: Load all collections
- `createCollection(name)`: Create new collection
- `updateCollection(id, name)`: Rename collection
- `deleteCollection(id)`: Delete collection
- `fetchCollectionClips(collectionId, append)`: Load clips in collection
- `loadMoreCollectionClips()`: Load next page of collection clips
- `resetCollectionClips()`: Clear collection clips state
- `addClipToCollection(collectionId, clipId)`: Add clip to collection
- `removeClipFromCollection(collectionId, clipId)`: Remove clip from collection

**Integration**:
- Collection clips respect filters from clips store
- Uses same pagination approach as clips store

### 4. Games Store (`stores/games.ts`)

**State**:
```typescript
{
  items: GameRow[];           // Array of { game: string, count: number }
  loading: boolean;
}
```

**Getters**:
- `games(limit)`: Get games list with optional limit
- `totalGames`: Total number of games

**Actions**:
- `fetchGames()`: Load all games with clip counts

**Data Source**: 
- Server aggregates from clips table
- Groups by game field
- Counts clips per game

### 5. Tags Store (`stores/tags.ts`)

**State**:
```typescript
{
  items: string[];            // Array of all unique tags
  loading: boolean;
}
```

**Actions**:
- `fetchTags()`: Load all unique tags from database

**Usage**:
- Tag autocomplete
- Tag filter selection
- Tag pattern matching

### 6. Batch Operations Store (`stores/batchOperations.ts`)

**State**:
```typescript
{
  selectedClipIds: Set<number>;  // Currently selected clip IDs
  isSelectionMode: boolean;      // Selection mode active
  lastSelectedIndex: number | null;  // For shift+click range selection
}
```

**Getters**:
- `selectedCount`: Number of selected clips
- `hasSelection`: True if any clips selected

**Actions**:
- `toggleClip(clipId, index)`: Toggle single clip selection
- `selectClip(clipId, index)`: Select single clip
- `deselectClip(clipId)`: Deselect single clip
- `toggleRange(clips, currentIndex)`: Select range from last to current (Shift+click)
- `selectAll(clips)`: Select all provided clips
- `deselectAll()`: Clear all selections
- `isSelected(clipId)`: Check if clip is selected
- `enterSelectionMode()`: Activate selection mode
- `exitSelectionMode()`: Exit and clear selections
- `getSelectedClips(allClips)`: Get selected clip objects

### 7. Toast Store (`stores/toast.ts`)

**State**:
```typescript
{
  toasts: Toast[];  // Active toast notifications
}

interface Toast {
  id: string;
  type: 'success' | 'error' | 'warning' | 'info' | 'confirm';
  title?: string;
  message: string;
  duration?: number;  // Auto-dismiss time in ms
  action?: {          // Optional action button
    label: string;
    onClick: () => void | Promise<void>;
  };
  onConfirm?: () => void | Promise<void>;  // For confirm toasts
  onCancel?: () => void | Promise<void>;   // For confirm toasts
}
```

**Actions**:
- `success(message, title?, action?)`: Show success toast
- `error(message, title?, action?)`: Show error toast
- `warning(message, title?)`: Show warning toast
- `info(message, title?)`: Show info toast
- `confirm(message, onConfirm, title?)`: Show confirmation dialog
- `remove(id)`: Dismiss toast

**Auto-dismiss**:
- Success: 3s
- Error: 5s
- Warning: 4s
- Info: 3s
- Confirm: Manual dismiss only

## Configuration (Not a Store)

The configuration is managed via `useConfiguration` composable using VueUse's `useLocalStorage`:

**Public Config** (persisted in localStorage):
```typescript
{
  viewMode: 'grid' | 'grouped';
  pageSize: number;                    // Default: 25
  autoPlayOnHover: boolean;            // Default: true
  showMetadata: boolean;               // Default: true
  dateFormat: 'relative' | 'absolute'; // Default: 'relative'
  enableKeyboardShortcuts: boolean;    // Default: true
  confirmBeforeDelete: boolean;        // Default: true
  compactMode: boolean;                // Default: false
  muteVideosByDefault: boolean;        // Default: false
}
```

**Private Config** (reactive, not persisted):
```typescript
{
  lastVisitedCollection: number | null;
  sidebarCollapsed: boolean;
}
```

**Usage**:
```typescript
const config = useConfiguration();
config.public.value.viewMode = 'grid';
```

## Store Patterns

### Request Cancellation Pattern
Used in clips and collections stores:
```typescript
if (this.abortController) {
  this.abortController.abort();
}
this.abortController = new AbortController();
this.requestId++;
const currentRequestId = this.requestId;

// ... make request with signal: this.abortController.signal

// Only update state if this is still the current request
if (currentRequestId === this.requestId) {
  this.items = data.items;
}
```

### Optimistic Updates
Some operations update UI immediately before API call:
```typescript
// Add to local state
this.items.push(newItem);

// Then sync with server
await apiCall();
```

### Normalized Data
Tags are stored as string arrays on clips, not as full objects:
```typescript
// Server sends: { tags: [{ id: 1, name: 'ace' }] }
// Client stores: { tags: ['ace'] }
```

